  "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs could personalize explanations—for instance, breaking down calculus proofs interactively. My philosophy interest aligns with their ability to scaffold abstract ideas (e.g., Fourier series). Gamify practice by turning derivations into puzzles, tapping my high agreeableness to foster collaboration. However, avoid over-reliance: my low conscientiousness score suggests structured checks remain crucial."
